  "term": "high-altitude cerebral edema",
  "definition": "High-altitude cerebral edema is a life-threatening brain complication of high altitude that can develop when acute mountain sickness gets worse. It is discussed alongside acute mountain sickness as a serious acute high-altitude illness.",
